<title>INDIA: India's 96/97 GDP growth estimates by sectors.</title>
<headline>India's 96/97 GDP growth estimates by sectors.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are estimates of the percentage change in India's gross domestic product (GDP) by sector for 1996/97 (April-March) and 1995/96 at constant 1980/81 prices released by the Central Statistical Organisation.</p>
<p> INDUSTRY			     YR/YR PERCENTAGE CHANGE</p>
<p>					  1996/97	   1995/96</p>
<p>1) Agriculture, forestry</p>
<p>    and fishing			 3.7		-0.1</p>
<p> 2) Mining and quarrying	    1.7		 7.0</p>
<p> 3) Manufacturing		    10.6		13.6</p>
<p>4) Electricity, gas and</p>
<p>    water supply			4.2		 9.1</p>
<p> 5) Construction			4.6		 5.3</p>
<p>6) Trade, hotel, transport</p>
<p>    and communication		 9.4		13.3</p>
<p>7) Financing, insurance,</p>
<p>real estate and</p>
<p>    business services		 6.3		 4.0</p>
<p>8) Community, social and</p>
<p>    personal services		 4.9		 6.2</p>
<p>    Total GDP at factor cost	6.8		 7.1</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
